<title>FINLAND: FINNISH SEPTEMBER EU-HARMONISED CPI RISES 1.2 PCT.</title>
<headline>FINNISH SEPTEMBER EU-HARMONISED CPI RISES 1.2 PCT.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Finnish consumer price index</p>
<p>partially harmonised to European Union standards rose 1.2</p>
<p>percent year-on-year in September after a 1.1 percent rise in</p>
<p>August, Statistics Finland (SF) said on Tuesday in a statement.</p>
<p>			September 1996     August 1996   Sept 1995</p>
<p> Yr/Yr			 +1.2 pct	   +1.1 pct     0.3 pct</p>
<p> Mth/Mth		     +0.2 pct	    N/A pct     0.1 pct</p>
<p> Index (base 1994=100)    102.3		102.1	  101.1</p>
<p>According to SF's regular national method of calculation,</p>
<p>Finnish consumer prices rose 0.2 percent in September on August</p>
<p>and rose 0.5 percent year-on-year, it said.</p>
<p>			    Sept 1996	August 1996    Sept 1995</p>
<p> Yr/yr		     +0.5 pct	    +0.4 pct	+0.3 pct</p>
<p> Mth/mth		   +0.2 pct	    -0.2 pct	 0.1 pct</p>
<p> Index (base 1990=100)  112.8		 112.6	   112.2</p>
<p>Six economists' average forecast for the national CPI figure</p>
<p>was for a 0.5 percent rise year-on-year and a 0.1 percent rise</p>
<p>month-on-month.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki Newsroom +358 - 0 - 680 50 245</p>
</text>
